ed, calculating production measurements, as necessary.","core":true,"importance":3.96,"relevance":77,"frequency":5.47},{"id":10284,"text":"Prepare metal surfaces or workpieces, using hand-operated equipment, such as grinders, cutters, or drills.","core":true,"importance":3.95,"relevance":91.31,"frequency":5.38},{"id":10292,"text":"Mark weld points and positions of components on workpieces, using rules, squares, templates, or scribes.","core":true,"importance":3.95,"relevance":81.99,"frequency":5.21},{"id":10286,"text":"Set dials and timing controls to regulate electrical current, gas flow pressure, heating or cooling cycles, or shut-off.","core":true,"importance":3.93,"relevance":72.87,"frequency":5.18},{"id":10266,"text":"Turn and press knobs and buttons or enter operating instructions into computers to adjust and start welding machines.","core":true,"importance":3.91,"relevance":77.68,"frequency":5.55},{"id":10275,"text":"Assemble, align, and clamp workpieces into holding fixtures to bond, heat-treat, or solder fabricated metal components.","core":true,"importance":3.91,"relevance":77.62,"frequency":5.57},{"id":10277,"text":"Conduct trial runs before welding, soldering, or brazing, and make necessary adjustments to equipment.","core":true,"importance":3.9,"relevance":78.25,"frequency":4.98},{"id":10287,"text":"Tend auxiliary equipment used in welding processes.","core":false,"importance":3.87,"relevance":62.33,"frequency":5.15},{"id":10269,"text":"Give directions to other workers regarding machine set-up and use.","core":true,"importance":3.86,"relevance":88.51,"frequency":4.76},{"id":10281,"text":"Select, position, align, and bolt jigs, holding fixtures, guides, or stops onto machines, using measuring instruments and hand tools.","core":true,"importance":3.83,"relevance":81.63,"frequency":5.21},{"id":10285,"text":"Clean, lubricate, maintain, and adjust equipment to maintain efficient operation, using air hoses, cleaning fluids, and hand tools.","core":true,"impor